# 1. Product Overview

**Product Name:** Company Brain — The Executable Knowledge Layer for AI Agents

Company Brain pulls a company's operational know-how out of the fragmented places it lives — people's heads, meetings, email threads, Slack, support tickets, internal docs, and databases — structures it into **executable skills**, keeps those skills current, and serves them to AI agents so they can do real work safely and consistently.

A *skill* is not a document and not a search result. It is a structured, executable procedure that captures **how the company actually does something**: how refunds get handled, how pricing exceptions are decided, how engineers respond to an incident. Each skill has a trigger, preconditions, steps, decision rules, guardrails, escalation paths, and citations back to the source evidence it was synthesized from.

Company Brain captures this knowledge two ways. **Passively**, it ingests the fragments work already leaves behind — meeting transcripts, Slack, email, tickets, docs, databases. **Actively**, every employee gets a personal **AI assistant (the Company PA)** that attends/ingests their meetings, tracks the commitments made in them, and follows up in plain human language — including a brief end-of-day conversation where the employee simply *talks* about what they did. No forms, no questionnaires. The PA is how knowledge that only lives in people's heads gets captured without it feeling like a chore imposed by the company.

Company Brain is explicitly **not** a company-wide search engine or a chatbot over documents. Those answer questions for humans. Company Brain produces machine-consumable skill files whose primary consumer is an AI agent that executes the work — fed by a continuous capture loop that keeps the underlying knowledge fresh.

> The blocker to automating a company is no longer model capability — it is that the domain knowledge needed to act is scattered, undocumented, and locked in human memory. Company Brain is the missing layer between raw company data and reliable AI automation.

