# 4. Scope of the System

## In Scope (V1)

### Fragmented source ingestion (live, incremental)
* Meeting transcripts (uploaded, or pulled from Zoom/Meet/Teams/Otter/Fireflies)
* Slack channels and threads
* Email threads (Gmail / Outlook)
* Support tickets (Zendesk / Intercom)
* Internal docs (Notion / Confluence / uploaded files)
* Structured databases (read-only connectors)
* **Company PA elicitation** — proactive, natural-language follow-ups and an end-of-day check-in that capture what only lives in people's heads

### Company PA capabilities
* Meeting understanding — extract decisions, owners, new features, and deadlines from transcripts
* Commitment tracking — first-class action items (who owns what, by when, status)
* Proactive follow-ups — natural-language nudges on open/overdue commitments (not forms)
* End-of-day check-in — a short conversation that turns "what I did today" into structured updates
* Per-employee assistant — each employee talks to their own PA in the app

### Core capabilities
* Procedure extraction — synthesize a workflow from many fragments
* Skill representation — structured, executable skill objects with citations
* Skill review & approval — human-in-the-loop editing and sign-off
* Freshness engine — contradiction detection, staleness flagging, re-extraction
* Skill-file export — agent-consumable files served via API
* Agent execution interface — agents fetch skills and report outcomes
* Safety — guardrails, required-approval steps, escalation, audit log

## Out of Scope (V1)

* General-purpose company-wide search
* A human-facing chatbot as the primary product (a review/Q&A assist UI is allowed, but it is not the deliverable)
* A **live "join-the-call" meeting bot** (V1 ingests transcripts; real-time attendance is a later enhancement)
* PA channels beyond **in-app chat** (Slack/email PA delivery is a later enhancement)
* Fully autonomous agents acting with no guardrails or approval gates
* Auto-execution of irreversible/high-risk actions without a human approval step
* Building the end agents themselves (we serve skills; agent runtimes consume them)
* Large-scale multi-tenant enterprise deployment

