# 5. Functional Requirements

## FR1: Source Connectors

The system shall ingest from fragmented, live sources — not only manual uploads.

| Source | Mechanism | Cadence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Slack | Events API / history pull | Incremental |
| Email (Gmail/Outlook) | Provider API | Incremental |
| Support tickets (Zendesk/Intercom) | API | Incremental |
| Docs (Notion/Confluence/files) | API + upload fallback | On change / on upload |
| Databases | Read-only connector | Scheduled snapshot |
| Human knowledge | Elicitation prompts (UI) | On demand |

Each ingested fragment retains source metadata (origin, author, timestamp, permalink) for citation and freshness.

## FR1a: Meeting Ingestion & Understanding

The system shall ingest meeting **transcripts** (uploaded or pulled from meeting tools) and:
* store the meeting (title, time, participants, raw transcript, summary);
* split it into per-utterance/segment **fragments** with speaker attribution;
* run extraction to identify **decisions, new features/initiatives, owners, and deadlines**.

A live "join-the-call" bot is out of scope for V1; transcripts are the input.

## FR1b: Commitment Tracking

The system shall treat **commitments** (action items) as first-class objects:
* `assignee`, `description`, `source` (meeting/fragment), `due_date`, `status` (open / in_progress / blocked / done / dropped), `last_followup_at`, `confidence`;
* commitments are created automatically from meeting extraction and from PA conversations;
* status changes are recorded as `CommitmentUpdate`s with the employee's own words preserved.

## FR1c: Company PA (Proactive Elicitation)

The system shall give each employee a personal assistant that:
* generates **natural-language** follow-ups grounded in that employee's open/overdue commitments and recent activity (never a form or fixed questionnaire);
* runs a short **end-of-day check-in** conversation — the employee describes their day in free text and the PA extracts structured updates;
* writes every captured update back as `Fragment`s and `CommitmentUpdate`s, feeding procedure extraction and freshness.

The PA conversation lives **in-app** in V1. The tone is a helpful colleague, not a compliance tool.

## FR2: Procedure Extraction Engine

The system shall synthesize **procedures** from fragments, not just entities.

### Workflow
```text
Fragments (many, contradictory, undated)
    ↓
Clustering by topic / procedure
    ↓
LLM synthesis → candidate skill (trigger, steps, rules, guardrails)
    ↓
Citation linking (every step traces to source evidence)
    ↓
Candidate skill queued for human review
```

Extraction must capture conditional logic and exceptions ("if order > $500, escalate to a manager"), not just a linear list of steps.

## FR3: Skill Representation

Each skill shall be a structured object:

| Field | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `name` / `description` | Identity and when-to-use summary |
| `trigger` | The situation that invokes this skill |
| `preconditions` | What must be true before acting |
| `steps` | Ordered, executable actions |
| `decision_rules` | Branching logic and thresholds |
| `guardrails` | Hard constraints; actions that require approval |
| `escalation` | Who/what to defer to when out of bounds |
| `citations` | Source fragments each element was derived from |
| `owner` | Accountable human |
| `status` | draft / approved / stale / deprecated |
| `freshness` | Last verified; contradicting-evidence flags |

## FR4: Freshness Engine ("keeps it current")

The system shall:
* Re-scan sources on a schedule and on new events
* Detect when new evidence **contradicts** an approved skill
* Mark affected skills `stale` and notify the owner
* Propose a re-extracted version for review

A skill is never silently changed; changes flow through review.

## FR5: Human Review & Approval

The system shall provide a review UI to:
* Inspect a candidate skill alongside its source citations
* Edit any field
* Approve, reject, or request re-extraction
* Assign an owner

Only `approved` skills are exported to agents by default.

## FR6: Skill-File Export (the deliverable)

The system shall export approved skills as agent-consumable **skill files** (Agent Skills / `SKILL.md`-style format) via API:

| Method | Path | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/skills` | List available skills (metadata) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/skills/{id}` | Full structured skill |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/skills/{id}/file` | Rendered executable skill file |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/skills/{id}/feedback` | Agent reports execution outcome |

## FR7: Agent Execution Safety

When an agent uses a skill, the system shall enforce:
* Guardrails and required-approval gates declared on the skill
* An audit log of which skill was used, by which agent, with what outcome
* Outcome feedback that feeds the freshness engine

