# 11. User Experience Flow

### Capture loop (Company PA)
```text
1. A meeting transcript is ingested → decisions + commitments extracted (with owners)
        ↓
2. The PA tracks each commitment and, when due/stale, sends the owner a
   natural-language follow-up ("how's the auth feature coming along?")
        ↓
3. At end of day, the employee opens their PA and just talks about what they did
        ↓
4. The PA turns that conversation into structured updates: commitment statuses
   change and new fragments are written to the knowledge base
```

### Skill loop (agent enablement)
```text
5. System extracts candidate procedures from accumulated fragments, with citations
        ↓
6. A human reviews, edits, and approves each skill
        ↓
7. Approved skills are exported as skill files via API
        ↓
8. AI agents fetch skills and execute work within guardrails
        ↓
9. Outcomes + new evidence feed the freshness engine; stale skills are re-proposed
```

---

# 12. Safety, Guardrails & Audit

* Every skill declares guardrails and approval-required steps.
* Agents cannot execute approval-gated actions without a human gate.
* Every agent skill-use is logged (skill version, agent, inputs, outcome).
* Skills are never auto-mutated; all change flows through review.
* Source-level permissions are preserved end to end.

---

# 13. Analytics and Reporting

### Skill metrics
* Skills extracted / approved / stale / deprecated
* Citation coverage
* Time-to-approval

### Execution metrics
* Skill usage by agents
* Execution success / escalation / failure rates
* Workflows fully automatable via skills

---

# 14. Security and Privacy

* JWT auth; role-based access control
* Source-level permission inheritance (an agent only sees skills it's entitled to)
* Encrypted storage and transmission
* Full audit trail of extraction, approval, and agent use

