# 16. Assumptions and Constraints

## Assumptions
* The knowledge exists across sources (and in people) even when undocumented.
* A human owner is willing to review and approve skills.
* An agent runtime exists to consume skill files.

## Constraints
* Procedure quality depends on source coverage and elicitation effort.
* High-risk actions require human approval gates in V1.
* We produce skills; we do not build the end agents.

